Found in read-only bug hunt (langertha-reviewer, 2026-09-25). REPRODUCED offline.

1) lib/Langertha/Role/OpenAICompatible.pm:429 reads $data->{choices}[0] with no check. A 200 body {"error":{"message":"upstream overloaded","code":502}} or {"choices":[]} yields Response content '' with no finish_reason and no error - indistinguishable from a legitimately empty reply. Gateways (OpenRouter and other proxies) are known to return error objects in 200 bodies (provider-reality: confirm with langertha-llm-advisor).
2) lib/Langertha/Engine/Gemini.pm chat_response: {"promptFeedback":{"blockReason":"SAFETY"}} (no candidates) -> content '' and finish_reason undef; the block reason is only in raw.
   Precedent: embedding_response already croaks with the error message on a missing data array (karr k171, OpenAICompatible.pm ~268).
   Fix: croak with the embedded error.message when the body has an error object and no choices; for blocked prompts set finish_reason from blockReason (or croak). Decide which and record it.
3) OpenAI structured-output refusals: message {content:null, refusal:"I can not help"} -> content '' and the refusal only in raw; Response has no refusal attribute. Per ADR 0004 a new field is a Response attribute: add refusal (Maybe[Str]) and surface it; Anthropic stop_reason refusal already arrives as finish_reason.
Also noted (declined, design): n>1 choices keep only choices[0] silently.
